{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'H4|unsupported increment|distinct from|already includ' docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window --glob '*.md' | head -60\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round22-brief.md:16:allow-list would stop a valid run); the reading rule (the primary line and its pass/fail/inconclusive; the harm lines, especially H4;\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PROBE-V2-RESULT.md:42:  forecast as incremental to an estimate that may already include it. Unmeasured: the probe bought no judgements.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37b-brief.md:26:5. **H4, read by me on all 71 post-link v14 forecasts of linked-1:** four answers add v8's CPU forecast on top of a total built from the\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round37b-brief.md:30:   §4 and §8, any double count is harm: with a valid control the pilot would still have stopped (H4). Please read the 71 v14\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/claude-r31.md:11:Read only the primary line by hand on that pair (about 144 pair classifications), with the H1/H2 code checks and H4's double-count\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r33.md:5:| Bind readings to the accepted stores | **Partly fixed.** P, H4, and gain rows are checked against regenerated evidence. The official entry point refuses dry summaries. The reader annotations can still claim work the packet does not substantiate. [P binding](verdict.py:77) · [H4 and gain binding](verdict.py:286) · [Paid-summary check](verdict.py:310) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r33.md:7:| Check coverage before confirmed harm | **Fixed.** With 58 readable linked dates and an H4 double-count finding, the pilot reports `inconclusive` for short coverage. The control floor follows the harm checks, as §4 specifies. [Precedence](PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [Pilot order](verdict.py:328) · [Dry result](e2e-checks.log:509) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r33.md:11:1. **Require the recorded reading, as well as the right source row.** On the dry stores, I replaced the first and second P and H4 readings with `false` and `7`, kept a valid final label as the third reading, and used excerpts absent from the source. The pilot continued. It also continued with each gain’s review reduced to `material failure: false` and `cpu increment: none`. Check each reading against its allowed values, bind excerpts to the supplied text, and require source-backed adjudication and a recorded Rule B trace for each supplying answer. Code can verify those records are present and tied to the source. Readers still judge what the source means. [Reading checks](verdict.py:50) · [H4 validation](verdict.py:323) · [Gain review fields](worksheet.py:253) · [Reading rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:141)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round26-brief.md:3:increment's quantified removal or unresolved bounds; H4 and H5 reaching P only through it; H1 harm at 4 or more; the reading load per\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r35.md:5:- **Disputed readings require a source.** Boolean and whitespace placeholders are refused. P and pilot H4 quotes are tied to the regenerated rows. The full verdict also checks quotes against regenerated H rows and rejects duplicate keys. Gain reviews now require quoted inputs and a written explanation. [Reading validation](verdict.py:50) · [Pilot H4 check](verdict.py:361) · [Full H-row check](verdict.py:416) · [Gain review check](verdict.py:276)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r22.md:13:3. **Make the harm checks cover the ways the chain can appear to improve.** For H4, read **every** post-link `v14` answer against the exact CPU conclusion it received and its paired fresh control. Check its reference, forecast and arithmetic whether or not `v8` is cited. Adding the whole CPU forecast to a company estimate that already includes it is harm. A supported increment over the amount already included is a different case. Record unresolved overlap explicitly. For H3, use keyword hits to guide reading and trace claimed market figures to outside statements of the right scope. The existing `unsourced` scan searches the dependency block, so copying a system forecast can clear it. Give a material arithmetic or sourcing error found in the July-style review an effect on the verdict. Restore the per-link report of relation, direction and sign, with the known weak CPU link disclosed. Finally, separate model refusals from infrastructure stops and give H1 an explicit comparison unit and denominator. [Harm rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:68) · [Reference scan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py:49) · [Per-link review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:167) · [July arithmetic rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reading-rule.md:5)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md:24:| H4: CPU double count in total revenue | **4 answers** (07-15, 07-16, 07-17, 07-18; in force 07-15..07-19) | no CPU link | Claude read all 71 post-link v14 answers; Codex did a shuffled second read with dates hidden (exploratory, because the list was in the brief); both lists agree |\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md:33:### H4\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/round31-brief.md:7:   machinery? Which open round-30 findings would also block a one-pair pilot read only on P, H1, H2 and H4?\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r20.md:11:**`v14 reads v8` is weak, with plausible downstream harm.** The seq-148 request gave the total a direct **$393B FY2027** estimate. The CPU card showed its ladder and Intel and AMD market shares. It supplied no full-year NVIDIA CPU forecast in the evidence shown to the matcher. If both directions would help, the tie-break favours the CPU question reading the total. The broad total also gives the CPU question little useful constraint, so `neither` is defensible. The positive sign is arithmetically plausible if other sales hold fixed. The risk is that the total treats an uncertain CPU forecast as incremental to a company estimate that may already include those sales. The probe bought no judgements, so that harm remains unmeasured. [Seq-148 request record, archive call 8741](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/probe-v2-1/census.json:455) · [Evidence shown to the matcher](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Tie-break](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:16)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:96:  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:101:  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:129:- **H4, the CPU link:** every post-link v14 answer in the linked sequences is read against the exact CPU conclusion it received and\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:138:H4 double count, H5) → fail; (4) **untestable** (a control with D_C < 2) → inconclusive, \"the class did not recur\"; (5) **P**: all three\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:143:arm name, P rows only) for the blind reader, and the H packet (H3, H4, H5 rows, which reveal the arm through their requests); the gain\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:149:the FY2027 low and high ends as each answer finally states them, the excerpt they come from, the class, a note. H3, H4 and H5 rows carry\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:154:outcome, an H3 or H4 finding, or an H5 mark goes to a third, source-backed read whose class decides. Reading load on old-2's schedule:\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:156:an H4 finding is made), 168 H5 marks (84 question-dates twice), the H3 traces, and the full gain review (both supplying answers of every\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:181:   flagged and unflagged stored answers: §4, `parser-validation.md`. 3. H4 on every post-link v14 answer; H3 traced outside the\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:187:link to the outside statement: §4 H3. H1 second refusal, H2 invalidates, H4 and H5 consequences in P, disagreement resolution,\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:192:control's conclusion in force: §4. The worksheet, its worked example, adjudication for P, H3, H4 and H5, reading time: §4.\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:194:adjusted, by one credit rule; H4 and H5 reach P only through it; H1's boundary stated (harm at 4); reading load counted per reader:\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:205:the blind P rows of both arms read by hand and bound to the stores' pairs; H4 on every post-link v14 answer of linked-1; H1 from the\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:207:refusal fails; an invalid run, coverage short or control-1 under 2 definite dates is inconclusive; an H1 or H4 harm stops; \"improved\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r23.md:14:4. **Resolve H1–H5 and verdict precedence.** H1’s threshold is usable as an explicit tolerance. A reader whose correction is also refused is a product failure and must have a defined outcome even though replay stops. For H2, an unexplained non-reader request or substantive output difference invalidates the fixed-trajectory comparison. For H4, keep the review of every `v14` answer, and make unresolved CPU overlap consequential when the unexplained uplift supplies the apparent reconciliation. H5’s tolerance of one extra material failure per pair could likewise let a single unsupported, carried-forward forecast drive P. Define the question-date unit and how reader disagreements are resolved. A material error that supplies the apparent gain must prevent a pass. Write the precedence explicitly for confirmed harm, an invalid or incomplete run, and a completed comparison that misses P. [Outcome and harm rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:71) · [Second-refusal path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:340)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r25.md:1:**NOT READY.** Version 4 fixes the handling of unresolved dates and linked double refusals. The remaining blocker is how P gives or withdraws credit for a gain. Two readers can apply the current wording to the same forecasts and reach opposite verdicts. [Credit rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:79) · [H4 and H5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:114)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r25.md:6:2. **Use one rule for withdrawing credit.** H5 currently turns affected linked overlap or clear dates into definite dates, even where the control was also clear. A material error shared by both arms could therefore make linked P fail without any difference on those dates. Limit P adjustments to actual gains. For H4, say explicitly that removing a quantified unsupported CPU increment determines the **credit-adjusted** class. If the increment cannot be quantified and could decide the verdict, use the unresolved bounds. Keep the original forecast class, and keep confirmed double counting as harm. The fixed H5 sample still supplies its separate paired harm count. [Credit rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:88) · [H4 and H5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:114)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r31.md:7:The recurring problem is broader than harm selection. It is the handoff from a run to a decision. Rounds 24–27 settled what an answer can earn credit for. Rounds 29–30 found that the implementation could accept incomplete or misidentified reading records. For the pilot, the open findings are the completed calendar, the binding of P and gain reviews to the actual judgements, and the two gain-credit defects. H3’s selector and paired follow-up, and H5’s duplicate-counting defect, can wait for the full reading. H4 checks double counting along the CPU link. The source and attribution harm in H3 remains unmeasured by the pilot. [Round 24](codex-r24.md:5) · [Round 25](codex-r25.md:5) · [Round 26](codex-r26.md:9) · [Round 27](codex-r27.md:3) · [Round 29](codex-r29.md:9) · [Round 30](codex-r30.md:9) · [H3–H5](PAID-DESIGN.md:115)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r31.md:13:Write the stopping rule more precisely than “not fewer.” Apply the existing precedence. A linked double refusal is a failure. An invalid run, insufficient coverage, or a control with fewer than two known definite dates is inconclusive at its prescribed step. With valid, readable, testable data, **not improved** means even the most favourable completion cannot show a reduction. **Undecided** means unresolved dates could change the result. Both stop further spending under this staged rule, with their different reasons recorded. Continue only if the pair still improves after the gain review and H1 and H4 clear. One pair can justify buying the rest. Acceptance still needs all three pairs. [Pilot wording](claude-r31.md:12) · [Bounds and credit](PAID-DESIGN.md:83) · [Verdict precedence](PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [AGENTS §7.3](../../../AGENTS.md:336)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r31.md:20:2. **Bind the pilot readings to those accepted stores.** Rebuild the expected P rows from both stores and check the supplying judgement IDs and date spans. Keep P blind through classification. Require one completed H4 finding for every post-link `v14` answer, with the CPU judgement shown in its accepted request and the control’s conclusion in force. Derive H1 from the dated summaries on matched reader-days. Demonstrate that a substituted P judgement or a missing H4 reading cannot produce a decision to continue. [P row builder](worksheet.py:80) · [P validation](verdict.py:41) · [H4 rows](worksheet.py:150) · [H1 calculation](verdict.py:146)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r37b.md:9:- **The reverse link produced four CPU double counts.** I shuffled all 71 answers, hid their dates and IDs, and marked four before restoring them. Your list was already in the brief, so this is an exploratory second read. My list matched yours: **July 15 (118), July 16 (134), July 17 (150), and July 18 (153)**. Each added $19–19.5B to a roughly $387B company-wide forecast without showing that the baseline excluded CPU sales. All four crossed $400B because of that addition, and the last held through July 19. July 20 reversed it. The “63 omit CPU” count applies to the forecast field alone. Across forecasts and reasons, **only three omit CPU or v8**. Any one confirmed double count would have stopped a valid pilot under H4. [Linked archive](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/linked-1-copy/archive.sqlite) · [H4 rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:129)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r34.md:3:1. **A disputed reading can be settled without a source.** `readings_complete` checks that `third source` has a truthy value. I supplied `true` for a disputed P reading and spaces for a disputed H4 finding, then used the third finding to clear an H4 double-count disagreement. The pilot continued. Require an actual quote tied to the regenerated evidence for the disputed finding. The full verdict uses the same check and matches its H rows by key, so its quote check should also use regenerated evidence rather than text carried in the submitted row. The gain check now requires a quote, but the dry fixture satisfies it by copying the first nine characters of the forecast. The gain review needs to record how its quoted inputs support the Rule B finding. [Adjudication rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:147) · [Reading validation](verdict.py:50) · [Pilot H4 check](verdict.py:431) · [Full H-row check](verdict.py:485) · [Gain fixture](e2e_checks.py:158)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r30.md:14:I reproduced **90 structural hits** on old-2, rising to **106 distinct rows** once fixed dates are included. That projects **636 H3 rows** over six similar sequences before extra linked hits and paired-control follow-ups. I would budget **18–30 reviewer-hours** for the full protocol, separate from the roughly three-hour run. That assumes 20–30 seconds for each of the 864 dry-schedule P marks, 30–60 seconds per H3 trace at roughly 700 rows, and additional time for H4, both H5 reads, gain review, and adjudication. The design’s **8–12 hours** is too tight for that workload. Recount after fixing H3 and time a representative batch before sending. [H3 load](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/h3-load.log:1) · [Protocol workload](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:141)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r26.md:5:Both fixes hold. Every gain in a provisionally improved pair now gets Rule B review of both supplying judgements. If the control has two definite dates and both linked gains lose credit, the result is a tie. Only gain dates can be adjusted, so a material error shared by both arms on a clear date leaves P unchanged. H4 double counting and the H5 sample retain their separate harm checks. Both verdict checks are specified in §7. [Credit rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:89) · [H4 and H5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:119) · [Verdict checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:178)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r24.md:16:I counted **72 distinct v9/v14 answer pairs** on old-2’s 73 dates. Budget up to **438 pair classifications** across six sequences, about **213 linked v14 reviews** on the stored schedule, and **168 first and second H5 marks** before adjudication. The workload is feasible, but the protocol is incomplete. Before launch, pin a worksheet keyed by judgement IDs and date spans. Give readers the full forecast text, the endpoints and excerpt to record, and the exact request and dated sources for harm checks. Apply source-backed adjudication to verdict-changing disagreements in P, H3 and H4 as well as H5. The old-1 September 8 case, **$419B against $414–421B**, is a useful worked example of overlap. The roughly three-hour estimate covers the model run. Reader time needs its own estimate. [Hand-reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:68) · [Overlap example](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/parser-validation.txt:35) · [Run time](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:126)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r36.md:7:I found no remaining path in the reviewed pilot that returns `continue` without two accepted runs, the required P and H4 readings, and complete gain reviews. Continuation still requires credited improvement with H1 and H4 clear. [Pilot decision](verdict.py:348) · [Continuation rule](verdict.py:387)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r32.md:1:**NOT READY.** The completed-calendar check is fixed. On the real dry stores, I still got `continue` with the forecast text, ranges, and source excerpts removed. I also got `continue` with a mismatched H4 request and with an invalid CPU correction that should have been refused. [Pilot decision](verdict.py:247) · [D708](../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10631)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r32.md:6:- **Readings bound to the stores — partly fixed.** `bind_p` checks the two judgement IDs and their exact dates. The H4 builder produced all 71 expected rows, each with the CPU snapshot and a paired control answer. But the decision checks only H4 judgement IDs and finding labels. I replaced the CPU ID and request and removed the paired control answer from one row. It still continued. P likewise accepted `clear` with a **$420B** segment and a **$400B** company, and minimal gain rows containing only IDs and verdict fields were enough to continue. [P binding](verdict.py:41) · [H4 construction](worksheet.py:150) · [H4 validation](verdict.py:262) · [Gain validation](verdict.py:202)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r32.md:11:1. **Accept reader findings against the evidence regenerated from the accepted runs.** Bind P, H4 and gain findings to their full expected rows, including the exact request and upstream and control judgements where required. Require the recorded reading fields and any required adjudication. Reject missing, substituted, duplicate or unexpected rows. The official pilot decision should require paid pair-1 summaries. The current entry point gives the same `continue` on accepted dry summaries. [Packet contract](PAID-DESIGN.md:141) · [Pilot packet builder](worksheet.py:215) · [Gain packet builder](worksheet.py:233) · [Summary and packet checks](verdict.py:247)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/codex-r32.md:13:3. **Apply coverage before harm, as §4 prescribes.** With the linked arm below 60 resolved dates and an H4 double-count mark, I got `stop` for confirmed harm. The prescribed result is `inconclusive` for insufficient coverage. Both halt spending, but they tell Alex different things about the product. Keep linked double refusal first, then check validity and coverage, then harm, then the control floor and credited P. [Verdict precedence](PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [Pilot branch order](verdict.py:247)\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:55:   with the exact requests, the read judgement ids shown and the paired control's conclusion in force (H4), the seven fixed dates (H5),\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:71:P 432 rows; H4 213; H5 84; H3 1,521 in the dry run, an upper bound (every marker answer changes its reference); a real run's H3 count\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:80:   the paired control's conclusion in force), H4 (a double count), H5 (2 or more extra material failures) from the read rows; each gain's\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:89:specified: P rows only, an unread H row, an incomplete gain review, every gain withdrawn (not improved: fail), an H4 double count, a\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:106:  a missing H4 reading refused; an H4 double count stops; a quantified correction turning the gains definite stops as not improved; every\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:112:   stores' row; `bind_rows` compares each H4 row (request, read judgements shown and their trace, the CPU judgement, control-1's answer\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:121:removed, a class the ranges contradict, a P row without its second reading, an H4 row with another request, an H4 row without the control\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:122:answer, and a NaN corrected range refused; coverage short before an H4 double count gives inconclusive; the carried correction gives\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:123:clear on one date and definite on the other). One fixture of mine set only the final H4 finding, which the new record rule refused; the\ndocs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:148:Evidence: `e2e-checks.log`, 40 checks, exit 0 (new: a disputed P reading settled with `true` or spaces, a disputed H4 finding without a\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
