sales by the end of this fiscal year\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n    \"what\": \"sales of its stand-alone Vera CPU line\",\n    \"how_much\": \"$20 billion\",\n    \"period\": \"by the end of this fiscal year (FY2027)\",\n    \"status\": \"forecast\"\n   },\n   \"weight\": \"core\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"i289\",\n   \"weight\": \"optional\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"i295\",\n   \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n   \"input_id\": \"gnews:ecde98f04e1a057b56113670\",\n   \"tier\": \"party_statement\",\n   \"who\": \"NVIDIA management (Jensen Huang, Colette Kress, Toshiya Hari) at a Morgan Stanley non-deal roadshow, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n   \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n   \"meaning\": {\n    \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n    \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n    \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n    \"status\": \"claim\"\n   },\n   \"weight\": \"supporting\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"i296\",\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py:2:question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match.\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/questions-v1.json:833:   \"id\": \"q19\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import sqlite3,re,pathlib,json,collections\nscratch=pathlib.Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\ndef db(a,name=\\\"views\\\"):\n p=pathlib.Path(f\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{a}/prod\\\") if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else scratch/(a+\\\"-copy\\\")\n c=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/(name+\\\".sqlite\\\"))+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,id):\n row=db(a,\\\"archive\\\").execute(\\\"select request_json,answer_json from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n return json.loads(row[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"],json.loads(row[1])\npat=re.compile(r\\\"semi.?analysis|(?:h2|second.half).{0,55}(?:compute|data.center).{0,55}(?:above|premium|outperform|upside|uplift|beat)|(?:20%|20 percent).{0,55}(?:h2|second.half|compute)\\\",re.I)\nfor a,views in [(\\\"old-1\\\",[\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v5\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v15\\\",\\\"v40\\\"]),(\\\"old-2\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v17\\\",\\\"v21\\\",\\\"v35\\\"]),(\\\"old-3\\\",[\\\"v3\\\",\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v44\\\"]),(\\\"control-1\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v21\\\"]),(\\\"linked-1\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v21\\\"])]:\n co=db(a)\n for v in views:\n  rows=co.execute(\\\"select call_id,publication_day,rung,implied_outcome,reasons from judgements where view_id=? and call_id>? order by seq,judgement_id\\\",(v,0 if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else 8737)).fetchall()\n  hits=[r for r in rows if pat.search(r[\\\"implied_outcome\\\"]+\\\" \\\"+r[\\\"reasons\\\"])]\n  if hits:\n   print(\\\"GROUP\\\",a,v,len(rows),len(hits))\n   for id,day,rung,i,r in hits:\n    # show all amounts and treatment in context\n    if a==\\\"old-3\\\" and v==\\\"v3\\\" or re.search(r\\\"q3|third quarter|v14|v4\\\",i+\\\" \\\"+r,re.I) and re.search(r\\\"uplift|incremental|adds?|adjust|outperformance|premium|discount\\\",i+\\\" \\\"+r,re.I):\n     print(id,day[5:],rung,i.replace(\\\" billion\\\",\\\"B\\\")[:480])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import sqlite3,re,pathlib,json,collections\nscratch=pathlib.Path(\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad\\\")\ndef db(a,name=\\\"views\\\"):\n p=pathlib.Path(f\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/{a}/prod\\\") if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else scratch/(a+\\\"-copy\\\")\n c=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(p/(name+\\\".sqlite\\\"))+\\\"?mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ndef req(a,id):\n row=db(a,\\\"archive\\\").execute(\\\"select request_json,answer_json from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(id,)).fetchone()\n return json.loads(row[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"],json.loads(row[1])\npat=re.compile(r\\\"semi.?analysis|(?:h2|second.half).{0,55}(?:compute|data.center).{0,55}(?:above|premium|outperform|upside|uplift|beat)|(?:20%|20 percent).{0,55}(?:h2|second.half|compute)\\\",re.I)\nfor a,views in [(\\\"old-1\\\",[\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v5\\\",\\\"v8\\\",\\\"v15\\\",\\\"v40\\\"]),(\\\"old-2\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v17\\\",\\\"v21\\\",\\\"v35\\\"]),(\\\"old-3\\\",[\\\"v3\\\",\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v35\\\",\\\"v44\\\"]),(\\\"control-1\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v21\\\"]),(\\\"linked-1\\\",[\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\",\\\"v16\\\",\\\"v21\\\"])]:\n co=db(a)\n for v in views:\n  rows=co.execute(\\\"select call_id,publication_day,rung,implied_outcome,reasons from judgements where view_id=? and call_id>? order by seq,judgement_id\\\",(v,0 if a.startswith(\\\"old\\\") else 8737)).fetchall()\n  hits=[r for r in rows if pat.search(r[\\\"implied_outcome\\\"]+\\\" \\\"+r[\\\"reasons\\\"])]\n  if hits:\n   print(\\\"GROUP\\\",a,v,len(rows),len(hits))\n   for id,day,rung,i,r in hits:\n    # show all amounts and treatment in context\n    if a==\\\"old-3\\\" and v==\\\"v3\\\" or re.search(r\\\"q3|third quarter|v14|v4\\\",i+\\\" \\\"+r,re.I) and re.search(r\\\"uplift|incremental|adds?|adjust|outperformance|premium|discount\\\",i+\\\" \\\"+r,re.I):\n     print(id,day[5:],rung,i.replace(\\\" billion\\\",\\\"B\\\")[:480])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"GROUP old-1 v4 80 43\n1782 07-24 2 About $425B: carry the Q1 actual and Q2 guidance run-rate forward, then apply the existing estimate that second-half FY2027 data-center compute revenue will be 20% above Wall Street expectations only to that portion of revenue. This remains below the $431.2B rung-1 threshold.\n1924 07-26 2 About $425B. Carrying forward the revenue run-rate indicated by Q1’s $81.62B and Q2 guidance of approximately $91B, with the existing SemiAnalysis estimate that second-half FY2027 data-center compute will be 20% above Wall Street expectations, supports roughly $425B; that remains below the $431.2B rung-1 threshold.\n2727 08-03 1 About $445–455B, centered near $450B. Starting from the consensus reference, strong reported growth and the $91B Q2 guide support the run-rate; SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half data-center-compute upside and the Rubin ramp add upside, with only a discounted contribution from the $20B standalone-CPU target and the multi-year $1 trillion Blackwell/Rubin figure.\n2978 08-09 1 Approximately $435B. Q1 reported revenue and Q2 guidance, which is close to the Q2 market estimate, anchor the forecast near consensus; the specific estimate of second-half data-center compute revenue 20% above expectations supports an uplift, partly offset by China constraints and competitive risks, with only a discounted contribution from the $20B stand-alone CPU target.\n3224 08-11 1 About $440B: start from the roughly $392–393B reference, apply a discounted uplift for SemiAnalysis's estimate that second-half data-center compute revenue will exceed expectations by 20%, and include only part of the $20B standalone-CPU target. The Q3 estimate and current-quarter guidance support the revenue trajectory; the SpaceX target is not counted as firm FY2027 NVIDIA revenue.\n3293 08-12 1 About $440B. This carries forward the quantified second-half data-center compute uplift over Wall Street expectations and discounts the $20B standalone-CPU target; Q1 actual revenue, Q2 guidance, and the Q3 estimate are consistent with that run-rate, while multi-year and post-deadline targets are not counted in full.\n3403 08-13 1 About $440B for FY2027. Q1 actual revenue of $81.6B, Q2 guidance of $91B, and the $103.1B Q3 estimate total about $275.7B through Q3; the remaining forecast and carried evidence of H2 data-center compute strength support a full-year outcome above the $393B reference, but the SpaceX opportunity is discounted because its capacity target is mainly after FY2027.\n3464 08-14 1 About $440B: carry the reported Q1 and guided Q2 growth trajectory through FY2027, incorporate the analyst Q3 estimate, and apply the 20% second-half upside only to data-center compute, with the separately forecast $20B standalone-CPU contribution. This places the forecast above $431.2B without treating multi-period orders or SpaceX’s later capacity target as FY2027 revenue.\n3561 08-15 1 About $435B for FY2027. Starting from the market's roughly $392–393B expectation, the strong Q1/Q2 guide and Q3 estimate support a higher run-rate; I apply the 20% second-half compute upside only to that portion of revenue and include only a discounted share of the $20B CPU target because shipments start in Q3 and ramp in Q4.\n3612 08-16 2 About $410B. The reported Q1, Q2 guidance, Q3 estimate, and a 12% sequential carry-forward imply about $391B before applying the in-force 20% upside view only to second-half data-center compute and a discounted contribution from the standalone-CPU target.\n3767 08-17 2 About $410B. The reported Q1, Q2 guidance, Q3 estimate and a 12% sequential-growth Q4 assumption imply roughly $391B; a limited second-half data-center compute upside and discounted CPU/Rubin contributions support the higher central estimate, without applying those inputs to total revenue wholesale.\n3902 08-18 2 About $410B. Q1 reported revenue of $81.6B, Q2 guidance of $91B, the $103.1B Q3 analyst expectation, and Q4 carried forward at 12% sequential growth imply about $391B; the in-force, specifically second-half compute upside and discounted CPU/Rubin contributions support a modest uplift, while the new 2028 OpenAI capacity is not counted as FY2027 revenue.\n4037 08-19 2 About $425B: the Q1 result, BofA's $94–$95B Q2 estimate and $107–$108B potential Q3 guide, with 12% sequential growth carried into Q4, imply about $404B before a discounted uplift for stronger second-half data-center demand, CPU sales and SpaceX-related demand.\nGROUP old-1 v8 75 39\n6376 09-01 1 Q1–Q2 actual Data Center revenue totals $164.25B. Applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% uplift to the analyst-estimate H2 baseline implied by Morningstar’s $361B FY2027 estimate gives H2 of about $236.1B and FY2027 revenue of about $400.35B.\n6817 09-04 1 About $400B, marginally above the rung-1 boundary. Q1–Q2 revenue totals $164.25B; Q3 is approximately $99.9B using the $108B guidance midpoint and Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix. The earlier H2 estimate baseline of $196.75B, uplifted 20% in SemiAnalysis’s H2 forecast, implies about $236.1B for H2 and roughly $400.4B for FY2027.\n7281 09-08 1 About $419B: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25B; Q3’s $108B total-revenue guidance midpoint at the recent 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9B. Carrying that sequential growth into Q4 gives an H2 analyst baseline of about $212B; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254B for H2 and approximately $419B for FY2027.\n7394 09-09 1 About $419B: Q3 Data Center revenue is estimated at $99.9B from the $108B total-revenue midpoint and 92.5% mix; carrying that sequential growth into Q4 gives an analyst-baseline H2 of about $212B. SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254B in H2, plus $75.25B in Q1 and $89B in Q2.\n7600 09-10 1 Approximately $418B: reported Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue sum to $164.25B; Q3 implies about $99.9B from the $108B total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% mix; the carried-forward H2 baseline of about $212B, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s forecast, implies roughly $254B for H2.\n7763 09-11 1 About $418B: the carried H2 analyst baseline of roughly $212B, increased 20% per SemiAnalysis’s forecast, gives about $254B for H2; adding Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue of $75.25B and $89.0B gives about $418B for FY2027. Q3’s $108B total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9B, so the H2 estimate requires roughly $154B in Q4.\n8321 09-15 1 About $418B for FY2027: $75.25B in Q1 plus $89.0B in Q2, about $99.9B in Q3 using the $108B guidance midpoint and 92.5% Data Center mix, and approximately $154B in Q4 implied by the carried H2 analyst baseline adjusted for SemiAnalysis’ 20% upside forecast.\n8613 09-17 1 About $418B: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25B; applying the latest 92.5% mix to the $108B Q3 total-revenue outlook implies about $99.9B for Q3. The carried H2 estimate, uplifted by the cited 20% SemiAnalysis view, is about $254B for Q3–Q4 combined, leaving roughly $154B for Q4 and putting the FY2027 total above $400B.\nGROUP old-2 v9 74 43\n4437 08-25 2 Approximately $417B: start with reported Q1 revenue of $75.25B and the $86.3B Q2 estimate, carry the approximately 14.7% sequential increase into Q3 and Q4, then apply SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside to the resulting H2 run-rate.\n4944 08-26 2 Q1 and Q2 reported Data Center revenue totals $164.25B. Applying Q2’s 92.5% Data Center share to the $108B Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100B for Q3; carrying the roughly 12% sequential increase into Q4 gives a roughly $212B H2 baseline, and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 outperformance forecast implies about $254B for H2 and approximately $419B for FY2027.\n5139 08-27 2 Approximately $417B: the $372B reference less Q1 actual revenue of $75.25B and the Q2 estimate of $85.8B implies about $211B of H2 estimates; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast gives about $253B for H2. Adding Q1 actual revenue and Q2 actual revenue of $89B yields about $417B. The $108B Q3 total-revenue guide, applied to the recent roughly 92.5% Data Center share, implies about $100B of Q3 Data Center revenue, leaving the forecast dependent on a strong Q4.\n5473 08-28 2 Approximately $419B for FY2027: $164.25B in the first half, about $100B in Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guide and recent segment mix, and roughly $112B in Q4 if Q3 sequential growth carries forward. Applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half outperformance forecast to that roughly $212B baseline implies about $254B in the second half and about $418B for the year.\n5598 08-29 2 Approximately $422B: $164.25B in Q1–Q2, about $100B in Q3 using the $108B total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and a roughly $115B Q4 estimate reflecting management's stated Q4 reacceleration. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% second-half outperformance forecast to the roughly $215B baseline second half gives about $258B for H2 and about $422B for FY2027 overall.\n5752 08-30 2 Approximately $422B for FY2027: $164.25B actual in Q1–Q2, about $99.9B in Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guide at the recent 92.5% Data Center mix, and an estimated $115B in Q4; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast to the roughly $215B H2 baseline yields about $258B for H2.\n5967 08-31 2 Approximately $422B: $164.25B in Q1–Q2 plus about $258B in H2, applying SemiAnalysis's 20% outperformance forecast to an approximately $215B H2 analyst baseline. The H2 baseline is consistent with about $99.9B in Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guide at a 92.5% Data Center mix and roughly $115B in Q4.\n6195 09-01 2 Approximately $422B for FY2027: $164.25B from Q1–Q2 plus an implied roughly $99.9B in Q3 and the carried roughly $115B Q4 estimate gives an H2 baseline near $215B; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate yields about $422B for the year.\n6218 09-02 2 About $422B for FY2027: $164.25B reported in Q1–Q2, about $99.9B implied for Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, and the carried Q4 baseline of about $115B make an H2 analyst baseline near $215B. Applying SemiAnalysis's estimate that H2 Data Center revenue will exceed analyst estimates by 20% gives about $258B for H2 and roughly $422B for FY2027.\n6405 09-03 2 About $422B: Q1 and Q2 total $164.25B; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9B by applying the reported 92.5% Q2 Data Center mix to the $108B total-revenue outlook; with the carried Q4 baseline of about $115B, H2 is about $215B. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside to estimates gives roughly $258B for H2 and $422B for FY2027.\n6599 09-04 2 About $422B for FY2027: $164.25B actual in Q1–Q2, about $99.9B implied for Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guide at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115B yield an H2 baseline near $215B. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate gives roughly $258B for H2 and about $422B for the year.\n6702 09-05 2 About $422B for FY2027: $164.25B of Q1–Q2 actuals, approximately $99.9B for Q3 from the $108B total-revenue guidance at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115B produce a roughly $215B H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast implies about $258B for H2.\n6867 09-06 2 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25B; applying the latest 92.5% Data Center mix to Q3’s $108B total-revenue guidance implies about $99.9B for Q3. Adding the carried Q4 baseline of about $115B gives an H2 baseline near $215B; applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies roughly $422B for FY2027.\n6975 09-07 2 About $414B: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25B; Q3 is estimated at about $100B by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108B total-revenue guide. The $372B reference implies about $208B in H2; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside implies about $249B in H2 and approximately $414B for FY2027.\n7072 09-08 2 About $414B: Q1 and Q2 actual Data Center revenue sum to $164.25B; the H2 analyst baseline of about $208B, derived from the carried FY2027 reference, rises to roughly $249B under SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside forecast. The $108B Q3 total-revenue guide and latest Data Center mix imply roughly $100B for Q3, consistent with—not additional to—that H2 estimate.\n7178 09-09 2 About $413–414B: Q1–Q2 total $164.25B; Q3 is roughly $100B from the $108B total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix; the carried H2 baseline of about $208B, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis, is about $249–250B. The Q3 estimate is included within H2, not added again.\n7400 09-10 2 About $413–414B: $164.25B of reported FY2027 H1 Data Center revenue plus approximately $249–250B implied for H2 by the prior roughly $208B baseline and SemiAnalysis's 20% upside estimate. The approximately $99.9B Q3 calculation is included within H2, not added separately.\n7562 09-11 2 About $414B: $75.25B in Q1 plus $89.0B in Q2 equals $164.25B for H1; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% uplift to the carried-forward roughly $208B H2 baseline implies about $249.6B in H2, or about $413.9B for FY2027.\n7670 09-12 2 Approximately $414B: Q1 plus Q2 Data Center revenue is $164.25B; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9B from the $108B company revenue guide and the latest 92.5% Data Center mix. The prior H2 baseline of about $208B, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s H2 estimate, implies about $249.6B for H2 and roughly $414B for the year.\n7770 09-13 2 About $414B: $164.25B from Q1 and Q2 plus approximately $249.6B for H2, using the carried $208B H2 analyst baseline increased 20% by SemiAnalysis. The Q3 guide and current Data Center mix imply about $100B for Q3, which is part of H2, not an additional amount.\n7939 09-14 2 Approximately $414B: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total about $164.25B; the $108B Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100B of D